      <section className="section soon" id="soon">
        <div className="section-head"><p className="kicker">10 / 🔭 COMING SOON</p><h2>Special Focus + new releases</h2><p>Aug 15–Sep 7: direct Special Focus matches first, followed by a selective radar of new arthouse, international, Asian and cult-minded openings.</p></div>
        <h3 className="lane-title">🎯 SPECIAL FOCUS · NEXT 30 DAYS</h3>
        <div className="soon-grid">
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.solaris)}><span>AUG 21 → 25 · BAM ROSE CINEMAS</span><h3>Solaris</h3><p><b>Andrei Tarkovsky · 1972 · 167 min · DCP</b></p><p>The first of BAM’s two Tarkovsky anchors in Arthouse Sci-Fi. If the Aug 12 Metrograph screening is inconvenient, this multi-date run is the stronger backup plan.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.bam.org/film/2026/arthouse-scifi-solaris" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.stalker)}><span>AUG 22 → 26 · BAM ROSE CINEMAS</span><h3>Stalker</h3><p><b>Andrei Tarkovsky · 1979 · 162 min · DCP</b></p><p>A direct Special Focus must-track: Tarkovsky’s Zone is one of cinema’s great immersive spaces, and BAM gives it a five-day window rather than a one-off.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.bam.org/film/2026/arthouse-scifi-stalker" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.memoria)}><span>AUG 22 → 27 · BAM ROSE CINEMAS</span><h3>Memoria</h3><p><b>Apichatpong Weerasethakul · 2021 · 136 min · 35mm</b></p><p>Apichatpong’s film is unusually dependent on theatrical sound and patient communal attention. BAM lists this return on 35mm, making it one of the month’s strongest Special Focus appointments.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.bam.org/film/2026/arthouse-scifi-memoria" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.happyHour)}><span>AUG 22 · 2:10 PM · METROGRAPH</span><h3>Happy Hour / ハッピーアワー</h3><p><b>Ryūsuke Hamaguchi · 2015 · 317 min · DCP</b></p><p>Hamaguchi’s five-hour ensemble breakthrough is a serious time commitment, but this is exactly the sort of Special Focus repertory return that can disappear from NYC calendars for long stretches.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://metrograph.com/film/?vista_film_id=9999001933" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.itEnds)}><span>AUG 21 · IFC CENTER</span><h3>It Ends</h3><p><b>Alex Ullom · 2025 · NEON</b></p><p>NEON’s Aug 21 release traps four friends on an apparently endless road, an economical genre premise with exactly the cult-minded edge your distributor focus is meant to catch. IFC lists the opening for Aug 21; additional showtimes remain subject to the theater’s final schedule.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.ifccenter.com/films/it-ends/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.mulholland)}><span>AUG 29 · 10:30 PM / AUG 30 · 4:00 PM · METROGRAPH</span><h3>Mulholland Drive</h3><p><b>David Lynch · 2001 · 147 min · 35mm</b></p><p>A direct Special Focus bullseye, and 35mm makes this more than a routine Lynch revival. The Saturday late show has the nocturnal texture the film deserves; Sunday is the easier practical option.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://metrograph.com/film/?vista_film_id=9999002169" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.goodbyeDragon)}><span>AUG 30 · 11:15 AM · METROGRAPH</span><h3>Goodbye, Dragon Inn / 不散</h3><p><b>Tsai Ming-liang · 2003 · 82 min · DCP</b></p><p>A movie about the final screening in a dying movie palace, watched inside another movie theater: perhaps the most perversely appropriate way to revisit Tsai’s great elegy for theatrical spectatorship.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://metrograph.com/film/?vista_film_id=9999000006" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
        </div>
        <h3 className="lane-title">🆕 NEW RELEASE RADAR · NEXT 30 DAYS</h3>
        <div className="soon-grid">
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.howDivorce)}><span>AUG 21 · 6:40 PM Q&amp;A · IFC CENTER</span><h3>How to Divorce During the War</h3><p><b>Andrius Blaževičius · Lithuania · 2026</b></p><p>A marriage breakup collides with Russia’s 2022 invasion of Ukraine in this Sundance directing-prize winner. IFC’s opening-night 6:40 PM show adds a Q&amp;A with Blaževičius and was still offering tickets at this check; later Aug 21–27 times are still TBA.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.ifccenter.com/films/how-to-divorce-during-the-war/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.crowsWhite)}><span>AUG 26 · IFC CENTER · SHOWTIMES TBA</span><h3>Crows Are White</h3><p><b>Ahsen Nadeem · documentary</b></p><p>Nadeem’s deeply personal documentary enters a secretive Buddhist community on Mount Hiei and finds its unexpected center in a Slayer-loving monk. IFC confirms the Aug 26 opening; exact showtimes are not yet posted.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.ifccenter.com/films/crows-are-white/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.gandahar)}><span>AUG 28 · IFC CENTER · SHOWTIMES TBA</span><h3>Gandahar</h3><p><b>René Laloux · France · 1987 · animation</b></p><p>Laloux’s final feature is a surreal animated science-fiction cult object populated by metal armies, mutants and a time-bending giant brain. Janus and IFC’s Aug 28 return is unusually aligned with your appetite for formally adventurous cult cinema.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.ifccenter.com/films/gandahar/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
          <article className="image-card soon-image" style={cardBg(images.colony)}><span>AUG 28 · IFC CENTER · SHOWTIMES TBA</span><h3>Colony</h3><p><b>Yeon Sang-ho · South Korea · 2025 · zombie thriller</b></p><p>The Train to Busan director returns to outbreak horror, sealing a biology professor and other survivors inside a biotech conference as the infected mutate. IFC confirms the Aug 28 opening, making this the Asian genre release to keep highest on the radar.</p><a className="official-link" href="https://www.ifccenter.com/films/colony-3/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Official listing ↗</a></article>
        </div>
      </section>

